1
00:00:20,860 --> 00:00:25,040
The shining, ultimate paradigm

2
00:00:27,100 --> 00:00:30,980
lightly leaping over these hectic times

3
00:00:33,160 --> 00:00:37,420
diving into the city,
playing at being a hero

4
00:00:37,420 --> 00:00:39,660
I wanna time with you, wanna night

5
00:00:39,660 --> 00:00:45,080
so we keep wearing nothing
but the latest trends

6
00:00:45,080 --> 00:00:49,080
because the bare face is
what sells out instantly

7
00:00:51,700 --> 00:00:58,240
Everybody can do,
the dreams we set running never stop

8
00:00:58,240 --> 00:01:03,260
Let's go for applause tomorrow too, you are

9
00:01:03,260 --> 00:01:10,820
Everybody can do, even if we
stick out a little, it doesn't hurt

10
00:01:10,820 --> 00:01:17,740
holding onto restless curiosity,
strike on, strong and high

11
00:01:28,980 --> 00:01:30,720
My home

12
00:01:50,360 --> 00:01:52,020
Too slow, way too slow.

13
00:01:52,020 --> 00:01:54,200
Terai hasn't come yet?

14
00:01:54,900 --> 00:01:57,820
You're supposed to arrive ten minutes before the handover,
you know!

15
00:01:57,820 --> 00:01:59,320
What's he dawdling for?

16
00:02:00,460 --> 00:02:01,920
I can't take it anymore.

17
00:02:01,920 --> 00:02:03,440
I'm going out to eat.

18
00:02:05,100 --> 00:02:07,740
Ryo-chan, you're still on
duty for another five minutes!

19
00:02:07,740 --> 00:02:09,440
Don't nitpick.

20
00:02:09,440 --> 00:02:11,380
Sorry I'm late.

21
00:02:23,260 --> 00:02:24,080
Yes!

22
00:02:25,840 --> 00:02:27,740
No need to be so surprised.

23
00:02:29,180 --> 00:02:31,640
Sure, the carp does look like Terai, though.

24
00:02:31,640 --> 00:02:32,760
Don't be stupid!

25
00:02:33,060 --> 00:02:37,440
Terai's a guy whose body and face are like a meat bun,
not a carp!

26
00:02:38,280 --> 00:02:39,580
Even so...

27
00:02:40,200 --> 00:02:44,040
That's right! Terai would never be
without a photo of his family on him!

28
00:02:44,820 --> 00:02:45,860
In that case...

29
00:02:45,860 --> 00:02:48,220
Really! Terai's family is in it!

30
00:02:48,220 --> 00:02:51,840
Right? We always take a group
photo together once a week.

31
00:02:57,380 --> 00:03:01,100
Looking at it this way,
you can really tell he was originally Terai.

32
00:03:01,100 --> 00:03:02,860
What happened, Terai?

33
00:03:02,860 --> 00:03:05,220
The commute's been a bit of a pain,
you know.

34
00:03:05,220 --> 00:03:07,680
Didn't you say you bought a house?

35
00:03:07,680 --> 00:03:09,720
How long is your commute, anyway?

36
00:03:09,720 --> 00:03:11,780
Round trip, it's about seven hours.

37
00:03:11,780 --> 00:03:12,740
Seven hours?

38
00:03:12,740 --> 00:03:15,780
Wasn't the Chief's round trip five hours?

39
00:03:15,780 --> 00:03:18,020
Whoa, that's two hours
longer than the Chief's!

40
00:03:19,140 --> 00:03:23,660
That's just what happens when you try
to buy a detached house on my income.

41
00:03:24,420 --> 00:03:26,860
I usually get up before dawn.

42
00:03:27,240 --> 00:03:29,480
I feel bad waking up my family.

43
00:03:30,040 --> 00:03:32,800
I eat a simple meal of
leftovers from the day before.

44
00:03:33,340 --> 00:03:35,120
It's an hour by bike to the station.

45
00:03:35,600 --> 00:03:38,040
By the time the sun comes up,
I finally reach the station.

46
00:03:39,900 --> 00:03:41,640
The trains are always packed.

47
00:03:44,040 --> 00:03:45,900
And I have to transfer five times.

48
00:03:45,900 --> 00:03:48,740
Miss one train and you're late, you know.

49
00:03:49,300 --> 00:03:50,380
It's desperate.

50
00:03:54,540 --> 00:03:56,200
Going there and coming back,

51
00:03:57,720 --> 00:04:00,100
and it repeats on the way back too.

52
00:04:00,100 --> 00:04:01,360
That's miserable.

53
00:04:01,360 --> 00:04:03,380
You'll wreck your body eventually, you know.

54
00:04:03,380 --> 00:04:06,480
But owning a home is
every salaryman's dream.

55
00:04:06,480 --> 00:04:07,940
Some sacrifice is

56
00:04:07,940 --> 00:04:08,280
No way.

57
00:04:09,280 --> 00:04:10,380
Sorry.

58
00:04:10,380 --> 00:04:13,340
If you at least try to
eat something nutritious,

59
00:04:13,340 --> 00:04:15,540
at this rate, your body won't hold up.

60
00:04:15,900 --> 00:04:18,157
Right, I was just about
to go get some food myself.

61
00:04:18,207 --> 00:04:21,900
Let's go eat something that'll build up our stamina.
Yakiniku or hot and sour soup or something.

62
00:04:22,040 --> 00:04:25,580
You're not planning to make Terai pay for it,
are you, Ryo-chan?

63
00:04:25,980 --> 00:04:26,520
Gulp.

64
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:31,700
I can't afford a meal that expensive.

65
00:04:31,750 --> 00:04:34,720
I've set my daily food budget at 350 yen.

66
00:04:35,640 --> 00:04:39,420
350 yen?!
That'll only buy you bread and milk at most.

67
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:42,040
Yeah, that's what usually happens.

68
00:04:42,200 --> 00:04:44,640
Yeah, 350 yen is more than enough.

69
00:04:46,080 --> 00:04:47,975
On a 350 yen budget, a full belly,

70
00:04:48,025 --> 00:04:50,100
I'll get you something
delicious to eat, Terai.

71
00:04:57,460 --> 00:04:58,560
Yes, welcome!

72
00:04:58,560 --> 00:05:01,000
Ryo-san, what can I get for you today?

73
00:05:01,320 --> 00:05:03,580
Right now, you're clearly lacking vitamins.

74
00:05:03,580 --> 00:05:05,740
You need to eat plenty of fruit.

75
00:05:07,460 --> 00:05:08,300
Apples

76
00:05:09,380 --> 00:05:11,480
At 350 yen, you'll blow your whole budget!

77
00:05:11,480 --> 00:05:14,380
These are fresh apples,
just delivered from the farm today.

78
00:05:15,900 --> 00:05:16,340
Liar.

79
00:05:18,480 --> 00:05:25,820
For apples delivered today, there's way too much dust on the stem end.
They've got to have been on the shelf for at least three days.

80
00:05:27,220 --> 00:05:34,900
Make it 200 yen. You can't beat mass production.
Fine, 200 yen is good, but the ones at the bottom are pretty bruised.

81
00:05:35,620 --> 00:05:37,020
This is worth 100 yen, tops.

82
00:05:37,600 --> 00:05:39,920
Fine. 100 yen is fine.

83
00:05:40,060 --> 00:05:42,060
Looking closer, there are bug holes in it.

84
00:05:43,100 --> 00:05:43,740
50 yen.

85
00:05:44,440 --> 00:05:45,580
Yes, that's fine.

86
00:05:45,860 --> 00:05:47,140
I can push him a little more.

87
00:05:49,720 --> 00:05:52,100
What's with this apple! It's hollow inside!

88
00:05:52,440 --> 00:05:54,340
H-hey, keep your voice down, Ryo-san.

89
00:05:54,660 --> 00:05:56,898
You're really going to sell
these totally hollow apples,

90
00:05:56,948 --> 00:06:00,000
to the housewives of Katsushika Ward?!

91
00:06:00,580 --> 00:06:03,000
What a terrible shop. I had no idea.

92
00:06:04,900 --> 00:06:05,980
Just take them, then.

93
00:06:06,680 --> 00:06:08,800
Well, why didn't you
say that from the start?

94
00:06:08,800 --> 00:06:09,940
Then I'll take them.

95
00:06:10,740 --> 00:06:11,820
No way, no way.

96
00:06:11,820 --> 00:06:14,460
Even at 500 yen, these are a bloodletting special,
I'm practically giving them away!

97
00:06:14,460 --> 00:06:16,440
Not a single yen off, got it?

98
00:06:16,440 --> 00:06:18,580
Damn, you're a stubborn one.

99
00:06:19,160 --> 00:06:20,060
Right.

100
00:06:20,520 --> 00:06:22,240
Speaking of which, you, last Sunday,

101
00:06:22,240 --> 00:06:24,100
you were in front of the off-track betting parlor,
weren't you?

102
00:06:24,560 --> 00:06:24,920
Gulp!

103
00:06:24,920 --> 00:06:28,520
Didn't your wife ban you from gambling?

104
00:06:28,520 --> 00:06:30,360
W-what are you talking about?

105
00:06:30,360 --> 00:06:32,120
Are you really going to play dumb?

106
00:06:32,120 --> 00:06:34,060
Ma'am! Actually, you see!

107
00:06:34,820 --> 00:06:36,300
Wa, wa, waa! Waa!

108
00:06:36,820 --> 00:06:38,800
Whoa! Big! Big!

109
00:06:38,860 --> 00:06:40,320
You! This is just a stopgap!

110
00:06:40,860 --> 00:06:42,780
No good, Naichia! Look, look!

111
00:06:42,820 --> 00:06:45,800
Pero pero bar! Anpapapapapapapa!

112
00:06:48,140 --> 00:06:49,960
Come on, Ryo-san, give me a break.

113
00:06:50,120 --> 00:06:53,440
My wife just finally came
back from her parents' place.

114
00:06:53,840 --> 00:06:55,780
Well, that's good news.

115
00:06:56,320 --> 00:06:57,800
So, how much is this?

116
00:06:58,420 --> 00:07:01,140
Fine, I'll let you have it for 300 yen.

117
00:07:02,420 --> 00:07:04,120
Ma'am, the truth is...

118
00:07:04,120 --> 00:07:07,180
50 yen, no, 30 yen is fine.

119
00:07:11,860 --> 00:07:12,920
Bring it over.

120
00:07:12,920 --> 00:07:14,280
I'll take it with me.

121
00:07:15,980 --> 00:07:16,760
Thanks for your business.

122
00:07:16,760 --> 00:07:18,060
Mass production is amazing.

123
00:07:23,280 --> 00:07:24,780
That was delicious!

124
00:07:25,780 --> 00:07:27,160
I'm stuffed.

125
00:07:30,400 --> 00:07:34,460
I never thought we could
eat this much on 350 yen.

126
00:07:34,460 --> 00:07:37,780
Since we ate together,
the cost was only half of that.

127
00:07:38,340 --> 00:07:40,180
This is all thanks to you, Ryo-san.

128
00:07:40,180 --> 00:07:43,100
Really, when it comes to haggling,
you're a genius.

129
00:07:43,100 --> 00:07:44,740
Call it shopping, not haggling.

130
00:07:44,740 --> 00:07:47,320
Nothing is too expensive
for me to bring down.

131
00:07:47,320 --> 00:07:50,740
When you buy your next house,
you should consult me, Terai.

132
00:07:50,740 --> 00:07:54,600
Didn't you buy your current
house after consulting Chief Ohara?

133
00:07:55,680 --> 00:07:59,000
Yes, Chief is the one who knows the most
about real estate at Katsushika Station.

134
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:01,620
I hear they call him the real estate demon.

135
00:08:01,620 --> 00:08:03,200
Real estate demon?

136
00:08:07,560 --> 00:08:09,520
And the result is a seven-hour commute?

137
00:08:09,520 --> 00:08:12,700
Consulting the Chief was
a mistake from the start.

138
00:08:12,700 --> 00:08:15,920
The Chief can't even buy a single
daikon radish properly on his own.

139
00:08:15,920 --> 00:08:18,920
A man like that could
never help you buy a house.

140
00:08:20,260 --> 00:08:21,880
Alright, back to work, back to work!

141
00:08:21,880 --> 00:08:23,740
Aitto, where are those documents?

142
00:08:24,800 --> 00:08:26,400
What's wrong with you two?

143
00:08:34,160 --> 00:08:36,580
So you were here.

144
00:08:36,580 --> 00:08:39,960
You were saying some rather arrogant things.

145
00:08:39,960 --> 00:08:43,160
No, I was just giving my
opinion as a shopping expert.

146
00:08:43,580 --> 00:08:45,220
A shopping expert, you say?

147
00:08:45,220 --> 00:08:49,780
Buying and selling real estate
is not like ordinary shopping.

148
00:08:49,780 --> 00:08:52,100
It's not as easy as you think.

149
00:08:52,540 --> 00:08:55,740
How so?
You still pay money to buy it, don't you?

150
00:08:56,840 --> 00:09:01,340
Then let me ask you: do you fully
understand the Real Estate Registration Act?

151
00:09:02,660 --> 00:09:05,040
The Real Estate Registration Act?

152
00:09:06,220 --> 00:09:08,420
Do you know the term
"building coverage ratio"?

153
00:09:08,600 --> 00:09:12,280
For large contracts, you'll also
need knowledge of the Civil Code.

154
00:09:12,280 --> 00:09:13,060
W-what about that?

155
00:09:13,420 --> 00:09:15,192
What about the Building Standards Act?

156
00:09:15,242 --> 00:09:17,520
And the Real Estate
Transaction Business Act?

157
00:09:31,580 --> 00:09:33,880
The Land Lease Act, the House Lease Act,

158
00:09:33,880 --> 00:09:37,280
the Act on Ownership of
Divided Units of Buildings,

159
00:09:37,280 --> 00:09:39,940
the Act on Virtual Collateral Contracts,

160
00:09:39,940 --> 00:09:43,040
the Constitution, the Penal Code,
the Commercial Code, the Accompanying Act,

161
00:09:52,320 --> 00:09:53,280
Don't be ridiculous!

162
00:09:53,940 --> 00:09:56,220
That kind of trivial legal
awareness is unnecessary.

163
00:09:56,220 --> 00:09:57,620
What do you mean, trivial?

164
00:09:57,620 --> 00:10:00,460
What would you know?
You've never bought a house.

165
00:10:00,460 --> 00:10:01,400
I know well enough.

166
00:10:01,400 --> 00:10:04,440
Anyway, Chief, your place is on
the outskirts of Chiba, isn't it?

167
00:10:04,440 --> 00:10:07,120
I chose my house for its surroundings.

168
00:10:07,480 --> 00:10:09,360
So Terai chose his house
for its surroundings too?

169
00:10:09,920 --> 00:10:12,320
There just weren't any
other suitable properties.

170
00:10:13,040 --> 00:10:14,040
It's your methods that are the problem.

171
00:10:14,440 --> 00:10:16,580
So you're saying you could find one?

172
00:10:16,580 --> 00:10:20,660
I'll find a house that's even more impressive than the Chief's,
and convenient for commuting.

173
00:10:20,660 --> 00:10:21,460
Interesting.

174
00:10:21,460 --> 00:10:22,860
Then, one week from now.

175
00:10:22,860 --> 00:10:25,340
Then you'll take me to the house you found.

176
00:10:25,340 --> 00:10:26,640
Bring it on.

177
00:10:26,640 --> 00:10:28,680
And if you can't find one, then what?

178
00:10:28,680 --> 00:10:31,600
I'll run a lap around Tokyo in the buff.

179
00:10:31,600 --> 00:10:32,120
Yeah.

180
00:10:32,940 --> 00:10:34,380
The deadline is one week from now.

181
00:10:34,820 --> 00:10:35,260
Got it?

182
00:10:35,260 --> 00:10:35,820
Ugh.

183
00:10:49,500 --> 00:10:51,100
Ryo-san, are you really okay with that?

184
00:10:51,100 --> 00:10:52,520
Making a promise like that...

185
00:10:52,520 --> 00:10:55,680
Well, I'd be happy if we found a better home than the current one,
but...

186
00:10:55,680 --> 00:10:57,200
I'm a professional shopper, you know!

187
00:10:57,200 --> 00:10:58,240
No need to worry.

188
00:10:58,240 --> 00:11:00,140
So, how about this shop?

189
00:11:00,140 --> 00:11:02,300
They advertise on TV all the time, but...

190
00:11:02,620 --> 00:11:03,100
Naive.

191
00:11:03,100 --> 00:11:05,780
Big real estate companies like
these are just like department stores.

192
00:11:05,780 --> 00:11:07,660
They have luxury and brand-name goods,

193
00:11:07,660 --> 00:11:09,800
but surprisingly few
options for ordinary folks.

194
00:11:09,800 --> 00:11:11,980
And above all, you can't haggle with them.

195
00:11:13,320 --> 00:11:14,260
Is that so?

196
00:11:14,260 --> 00:11:16,520
The best targets are in a
corner of the shopping street,

197
00:11:16,520 --> 00:11:19,680
shops that have been barely getting by for ages,
always on the verge of closing but never quite do.

198
00:11:22,980 --> 00:11:24,100
What kind of shop?

199
00:11:29,940 --> 00:11:32,660
That's exactly where
the bargains are hiding.

200
00:11:32,660 --> 00:11:33,940
Let's go, Terai.

201
00:11:35,300 --> 00:11:39,120
What do you mean we've only
got one contract this month?

202
00:11:39,120 --> 00:11:42,180
But we don't have any
decent properties to -

203
00:11:43,040 --> 00:11:45,120
Selling them is what makes a salesman's skill,
isn't it?

204
00:11:45,620 --> 00:11:47,060
Business is all about negotiation.

205
00:11:47,060 --> 00:11:48,800
Right on the edge of what's legal,

206
00:11:48,800 --> 00:11:50,560
it's all about how you
win the other side over.

207
00:11:50,560 --> 00:11:52,420
Chief, it looks like we have a customer.

208
00:11:57,860 --> 00:11:59,440
Alright, leave those two to me.

209
00:11:59,440 --> 00:12:01,720
I'll get them to sign that
contract no matter what.

210
00:12:01,720 --> 00:12:03,720
Smile, smile.

211
00:12:06,540 --> 00:12:07,560
Welcome!

212
00:12:08,100 --> 00:12:11,080
We sincerely meet the needs
of our valued customers.

213
00:12:28,060 --> 00:12:30,000
Sincerity has been my
only creed for forty years.

214
00:12:30,000 --> 00:12:32,360
I serve as sales manager at this shop.

215
00:12:32,360 --> 00:12:34,000
My name is Hanyu Tochiro.

216
00:12:34,460 --> 00:12:36,280
What kind of property are you looking for?

217
00:12:36,280 --> 00:12:37,580
What's your budget?

218
00:12:38,240 --> 00:12:40,420
About two and a half hours from Tokyo,

219
00:12:40,420 --> 00:12:43,140
I'd like a detached house
for around 25 million yen.

220
00:12:43,140 --> 00:12:45,240
So this guy's the buyer?

221
00:12:45,240 --> 00:12:46,780
He looks easy to take in.

222
00:12:48,300 --> 00:12:49,320
In that case,

223
00:12:49,320 --> 00:12:49,920
Wait.

224
00:12:50,600 --> 00:12:52,820
Then we can't impress the Chief.

225
00:12:52,820 --> 00:12:55,820
One hour from Tokyo,
and the budget is 15 million yen.

226
00:12:55,820 --> 00:12:57,500
Tch, what a noisy guy.

227
00:12:57,500 --> 00:13:01,140
Sir, you are incredibly lucky.

228
00:13:01,140 --> 00:13:03,180
Actually, it was just completed recently,

229
00:13:03,180 --> 00:13:05,800
and there's a property that
isn't even advertised yet.

230
00:13:05,800 --> 00:13:07,340
Just one hour from Tokyo.

231
00:13:07,340 --> 00:13:09,380
And the price is an
astonishing 3 million yen.

232
00:13:10,420 --> 00:13:10,760
Is there one?

233
00:13:11,280 --> 00:13:12,980
It's the result of pursuing sincerity.

234
00:13:12,980 --> 00:13:15,560
No other shop could ever hope to match that.

235
00:13:15,560 --> 00:13:18,220
This is definitely better
than Chief Ohara's house.

236
00:13:18,660 --> 00:13:19,880
It's an amazing find.

237
00:13:20,780 --> 00:13:23,180
Please sign the contract here right away.

238
00:13:24,020 --> 00:13:24,660
Y-yes.

239
00:13:26,040 --> 00:13:27,140
And that's that.

240
00:13:28,020 --> 00:13:28,860
Hold on a second!

241
00:13:29,700 --> 00:13:30,840
What's wrong, Rio-san?

242
00:13:31,140 --> 00:13:32,520
From my experience,

243
00:13:32,520 --> 00:13:36,200
a shop almost never offers its best
product to a first-time customer right away.

244
00:13:36,200 --> 00:13:39,360
There's probably a better
property than this one.

245
00:13:40,880 --> 00:13:42,220
W-what are you saying?

246
00:13:42,220 --> 00:13:45,980
Even for a first-time customer,
we always offer the finest properties.

247
00:13:45,980 --> 00:13:48,700
That's exactly why we're
known as the honest agency.

248
00:13:48,700 --> 00:13:51,840
That's right, a bargain property like
this doesn't come along every day.

249
00:13:51,840 --> 00:13:54,460
Chief, we found a better picture than yours,
so what's the problem?

250
00:13:55,160 --> 00:13:57,460
But I don't like buying something
just because it looks nice.

251
00:13:57,460 --> 00:13:59,780
There might be room for negotiation.

252
00:14:00,440 --> 00:14:01,900
Uh-oh, now we're in trouble.

253
00:14:02,500 --> 00:14:03,960
Whoops, I got the shakes.

254
00:14:05,320 --> 00:14:06,900
Hello, this is Seijitsu Real Estate.

255
00:14:08,160 --> 00:14:10,880
Good to hear from you,
thank you for all your help.

256
00:14:11,260 --> 00:14:12,340
Excuse me for a moment.

257
00:14:14,920 --> 00:14:16,180
That property?

258
00:14:16,940 --> 00:14:17,960
Please wait a moment.

259
00:14:17,960 --> 00:14:19,080
This is urgent.

260
00:14:19,580 --> 00:14:22,280
We just got a call from someone who
wants to buy that property right away.

261
00:14:22,980 --> 00:14:23,960
What would you like to do?

262
00:14:24,400 --> 00:14:26,440
If you're not satisfied, sir,

263
00:14:26,440 --> 00:14:29,240
we'll have to sign the contract
with this other party immediately.

264
00:14:29,240 --> 00:14:31,160
Understood, I'll sign right now.

265
00:14:31,160 --> 00:14:32,360
Hold on!

266
00:14:32,360 --> 00:14:34,040
Deal's done.

267
00:14:34,780 --> 00:14:36,729
I'm terribly sorry, but

268
00:14:36,779 --> 00:14:38,728
it has just been sold.

269
00:14:38,778 --> 00:14:40,920
I really am very sorry.

270
00:14:41,620 --> 00:14:42,720
Excuse me.

271
00:14:42,940 --> 00:14:44,080
Yes, what is it?

272
00:14:44,260 --> 00:14:46,140
Looks like my pen ran out of ink.

273
00:14:48,700 --> 00:14:51,159
I-I beg your pardon. Hey, Tsukamoto, pen,

274
00:14:51,209 --> 00:14:53,480
pen, hurry up and hand me a pen,
pen, pen, pen.

275
00:14:53,540 --> 00:14:53,680
Here.

276
00:14:56,340 --> 00:14:58,700
That panicked way of
acting is no ordinary thing.

277
00:15:00,040 --> 00:15:01,640
Show me that again.

278
00:15:10,160 --> 00:15:11,440
Yes, a pen, pen-pen.

279
00:15:11,440 --> 00:15:13,440
Let's just sign quickly,
let's sign, let's sign.

280
00:15:13,440 --> 00:15:14,800
3.0 tsubo?

281
00:15:15,140 --> 00:15:15,600
Gulp!

282
00:15:16,320 --> 00:15:17,620
It's 30 tsubo, Ryo-san.

283
00:15:17,620 --> 00:15:20,020
There's no way a house
could be that cramped.

284
00:15:20,020 --> 00:15:21,480
That's why something feels off.

285
00:15:21,480 --> 00:15:23,220
Hey, what's this pen about?

286
00:15:23,880 --> 00:15:27,540
Ink stains do sometimes end up on documents,
you know.

287
00:15:28,000 --> 00:15:30,180
See, you're overthinking it, Ryo-san.

288
00:15:30,180 --> 00:15:32,800
Then just to be safe,
how many tsubo is this house?

289
00:15:34,040 --> 00:15:35,200
Right, it's on this street, yes.

290
00:15:35,200 --> 00:15:37,560
I'm asking how many tsubo it is!

291
00:15:37,900 --> 00:15:40,080
On the street the customer is looking at,

292
00:15:40,080 --> 00:15:42,440
So you can't even say how many tsubo it is?

293
00:15:42,440 --> 00:15:43,950
Ryo-san,

294
00:15:44,000 --> 00:15:47,120
there's no need to force yourself this much.

295
00:15:47,120 --> 00:15:48,700
Don't you notice, Terai?

296
00:15:48,700 --> 00:15:52,080
This guy hasn't said a single
word about it being thirty tsubo!

297
00:15:52,080 --> 00:15:53,200
Now that you mention it...

298
00:15:53,200 --> 00:15:53,980
Gulp.

299
00:15:54,500 --> 00:15:55,960
Suspicious.

300
00:15:58,760 --> 00:16:01,980
If you can't say how many tsubo it is,
let's see the property itself.

301
00:16:01,980 --> 00:16:05,520
If you keep dawdling,
someone else will snap it up!

302
00:16:05,520 --> 00:16:07,740
Stop your yammering and just take us there.

303
00:16:08,360 --> 00:16:08,680
Yes.

304
00:16:14,820 --> 00:16:18,840
How about this wonderful
location and dazzling exterior?

305
00:16:18,840 --> 00:16:22,900
You won't find a better bargain
anywhere in the entire metropolitan area.

306
00:16:24,020 --> 00:16:25,920
So how are people supposed to live in it?

307
00:16:25,920 --> 00:16:27,980
Do people have to get blasted
with micro-rays to fit in?

308
00:16:27,980 --> 00:16:30,240
Was it really only 3.0 tatami mats?

309
00:16:31,980 --> 00:16:33,020
I almost got fooled.

310
00:16:33,020 --> 00:16:34,100
Can I really trust that?

311
00:16:35,280 --> 00:16:37,100
We have no intention of deceiving anyone.

312
00:16:37,460 --> 00:16:40,060
You show me a toy house like this and
then have the nerve to play innocent!

313
00:16:40,060 --> 00:16:43,440
I never once said it was a house for people.

314
00:16:43,440 --> 00:16:45,060
This is a house for pets.

315
00:16:45,060 --> 00:16:45,700
Pets?

316
00:16:50,280 --> 00:16:52,360
Among pet lovers these days,

317
00:16:52,360 --> 00:16:55,460
not content with the
shabby doghouses of old,

318
00:16:55,460 --> 00:16:59,620
more and more people are wanting
luxurious pet houses like this one.

319
00:17:00,140 --> 00:17:01,860
You're thoroughly suspicious, you know that?

320
00:17:01,860 --> 00:17:04,160
When I first saw you, sir,

321
00:17:04,160 --> 00:17:06,240
I was so sure you were a pet lover,

322
00:17:06,240 --> 00:17:07,600
that I jumped to the wrong conclusion.

323
00:17:08,280 --> 00:17:10,520
I am truly, truly sorry.

324
00:17:11,640 --> 00:17:14,340
As an apology, I'd like to offer you

325
00:17:14,340 --> 00:17:16,600
a super premium property nearby
at a sincere 50% off price,

326
00:17:16,600 --> 00:17:18,460
if you'd allow me to.

327
00:17:18,900 --> 00:17:20,580
So please, forgive me.

328
00:17:21,360 --> 00:17:23,540
First, let me see the actual property.

329
00:17:24,740 --> 00:17:25,780
I won't let you get away.

330
00:17:25,780 --> 00:17:28,000
You're going to sign at the next one,
no matter what!

331
00:17:36,180 --> 00:17:38,380
Please, take a look. That's the house.

332
00:17:39,360 --> 00:17:41,040
That's a pretty nice house, isn't it?

333
00:17:41,040 --> 00:17:42,140
How much is it?

334
00:17:42,140 --> 00:17:44,660
Normally,
it would be close to 20 million yen,

335
00:17:45,220 --> 00:17:48,100
but at our sincere price,
it's a straight 8.5 million yen.

336
00:17:48,100 --> 00:17:49,540
Really?

337
00:17:49,540 --> 00:17:54,280
Frankly speaking, if we sell it at this low a price,
the company will be deep in the red.

338
00:17:54,280 --> 00:17:54,840
But,

339
00:17:57,340 --> 00:17:59,220
the company's motto is sincerity.

340
00:17:59,620 --> 00:18:00,960
My motto is sincerity too.

341
00:18:00,960 --> 00:18:03,120
Sincerity is written with the characters for
"truth" and "fruit."

342
00:18:03,500 --> 00:18:06,720
To uphold our sincerity,
we're prepared to take a small loss.

343
00:18:06,720 --> 00:18:08,880
Sincerity Bazaar!

344
00:18:09,740 --> 00:18:12,560
Before other customers find out,
let's sign the contract right here.

345
00:18:12,560 --> 00:18:13,320
Quick, quick,

346
00:18:14,780 --> 00:18:15,860
Gotcha!

347
00:18:17,680 --> 00:18:18,320
Whoa!

348
00:18:18,380 --> 00:18:19,780
W-what are you doing?!

349
00:18:19,880 --> 00:18:21,760
Let me take a closer look.

350
00:18:21,760 --> 00:18:22,740
No, you can't! That's not allowed!

351
00:18:22,820 --> 00:18:23,580
I said it's not allowed!

352
00:18:23,680 --> 00:18:24,300
Stop it, stop!

353
00:18:24,420 --> 00:18:25,440
Why shouldn't I?

354
00:18:25,640 --> 00:18:27,380
That guy's hiding something again.

355
00:18:27,380 --> 00:18:27,600
I'm going!

356
00:18:27,600 --> 00:18:29,800
Ugh, anyway, you can't go!

357
00:18:41,720 --> 00:18:42,720
What is this?!

358
00:18:47,140 --> 00:18:49,360
Good grief, it's really not a livable house!

359
00:18:49,680 --> 00:18:52,680
N-no way! It's really livable, I swear!

360
00:18:54,420 --> 00:18:58,000
It has a Japanese-style room,
a kitchen, and a bathroom, all here.

361
00:18:58,620 --> 00:19:00,340
It's like an eel's bed.

362
00:19:00,340 --> 00:19:02,780
So a family of four has to sleep lengthwise?

363
00:19:04,000 --> 00:19:04,980
Greedy.

364
00:19:05,520 --> 00:19:09,140
At this rate,
you'd have to fit your body to the house.

365
00:19:09,740 --> 00:19:11,380
It's a spacious, roomy bathroom, right?

366
00:19:11,380 --> 00:19:15,120
But you'd have to go through the bathtub to get to the next room,
wouldn't you?

367
00:19:15,120 --> 00:19:16,600
That's quite enough.

368
00:19:19,060 --> 00:19:20,280
Rest assured.

369
00:19:20,280 --> 00:19:23,180
Yes, our company has
many sincere properties.

370
00:19:23,180 --> 00:19:26,080
I'm sure there's one
that will suit your taste.

371
00:19:26,700 --> 00:19:28,280
Not bad at all for a job.

372
00:19:28,280 --> 00:19:29,780
But this time, for sure.

373
00:19:30,660 --> 00:19:34,060
How about this? This spacious entrance.

374
00:19:34,760 --> 00:19:37,440
This is a dining kitchen designed
with functional beauty in mind.

375
00:19:38,640 --> 00:19:40,560
And this is the bathroom.

376
00:19:41,600 --> 00:19:43,700
What do you think of this
bright Japanese-style room?

377
00:19:44,960 --> 00:19:48,080
This house is 15 million
yen at our sincere price.

378
00:19:48,080 --> 00:19:50,300
For the city center, it's a bargain price.

379
00:19:51,040 --> 00:19:54,200
At this price, it's no worse
than the Chief's house, Ryo-san.

380
00:19:56,020 --> 00:19:56,780
An earthquake...

381
00:19:58,100 --> 00:20:01,560
Hey, who locks an apartment during an earthquake?
Open it right now!

382
00:20:01,560 --> 00:20:03,020
Was I supposed to open it?

383
00:20:03,020 --> 00:20:04,640
Move aside, I'll open it!

384
00:20:04,640 --> 00:20:06,000
No, you mustn't. I'll open it.

385
00:20:06,000 --> 00:20:07,860
Damn you, get out of the way!

386
00:20:07,860 --> 00:20:09,320
Wait a moment, please.

387
00:20:09,740 --> 00:20:11,620
I knew it,
you're hiding something again, aren't you?

388
00:20:12,140 --> 00:20:14,040
You're imagining things.
Just your imagination.

389
00:20:14,040 --> 00:20:16,300
Alright,
I'll force it open by any means necessary!

390
00:20:27,540 --> 00:20:29,820
This house is floating on the sea, damn it.

391
00:20:30,300 --> 00:20:32,520
It's cheaper because there's no land cost.

392
00:20:32,520 --> 00:20:33,860
Pretty stylish, isn't it?

393
00:20:34,320 --> 00:20:36,140
One typhoon and it'd be done for,
wouldn't it?

394
00:20:36,820 --> 00:20:38,600
The next property is definitely fine.

395
00:20:39,000 --> 00:20:40,900
In the sense that there's no land cost.

396
00:20:40,900 --> 00:20:42,460
This one's cheap too, though.

397
00:20:42,920 --> 00:20:44,600
No one could possibly
live in a place like this!

398
00:20:45,720 --> 00:20:47,420
I think I'm going to get sick.

399
00:20:48,880 --> 00:20:50,480
Please build it yourself.

400
00:20:50,480 --> 00:20:53,080
We've kept the price low
by cutting out labor costs.

401
00:20:53,080 --> 00:20:53,880
Hey, listen.

402
00:20:56,260 --> 00:20:58,260
Hiro, let's just give up already.

403
00:20:58,260 --> 00:21:00,940
There's no way we'll find a house
better than the chief's place.

404
00:21:00,940 --> 00:21:02,540
We're not going to find one that easily.

405
00:21:02,540 --> 00:21:04,300
If we give up,
that means I lose, doesn't it?

406
00:21:04,300 --> 00:21:06,880
I'm not letting the chief
get another big win over me.

407
00:21:06,880 --> 00:21:07,440
Hey.

408
00:21:07,440 --> 00:21:09,720
If it comes to this,
I'll overlook a few things.

409
00:21:10,340 --> 00:21:12,100
We're going to find a
better house than this one.

410
00:21:13,040 --> 00:21:14,820
I really will overlook a few things.

411
00:21:35,840 --> 00:21:37,900
This is our company's secret property.

412
00:21:37,900 --> 00:21:41,220
There is no better house in the Tokyo area.

413
00:21:41,220 --> 00:21:42,620
Lucky for you, Hanyu.

414
00:21:42,620 --> 00:21:44,840
It's a much better house than the Chief's.

415
00:21:46,000 --> 00:21:48,420
It's a bit of a concern that it
gets so little sunlight, though.

416
00:21:48,420 --> 00:21:49,920
"A bit"? That's an understatement, isn't it?

417
00:21:49,920 --> 00:21:51,840
Not even the trees get any sunlight,
do they?

418
00:21:51,840 --> 00:21:54,800
Why is there a house
underground in the first place?

419
00:21:57,440 --> 00:21:59,240
That's because there's no land cost.

420
00:21:59,240 --> 00:22:02,520
Apart from the sunlight,
this house is superior in every way.

421
00:22:02,520 --> 00:22:04,720
That's not the point, is it!

422
00:22:04,720 --> 00:22:07,040
Plus, it's convenient for commuting.

423
00:22:10,560 --> 00:22:11,940
The station is only one second away!

424
00:22:11,940 --> 00:22:13,820
And it even connects right to the platform.

425
00:22:14,840 --> 00:22:15,220
I don't know.

426
00:22:17,600 --> 00:22:22,220
Plus, gas, water, electricity, and phone are
all hooked up directly, so it's basically free.

427
00:22:22,800 --> 00:22:24,340
That's illegal, you know!

428
00:22:24,340 --> 00:22:26,980
Illegal or not,
it's better than the Chief's place.

429
00:22:26,980 --> 00:22:30,600
Are you even a police officer?

430
00:22:30,600 --> 00:22:33,380
Chief, no matter how you try
to dodge it by saying that...

431
00:22:33,380 --> 00:22:36,280
Why don't you just admit you lost to me?

432
00:22:36,760 --> 00:22:38,900
I'll knock that rotten attitude out of you.

433
00:22:45,540 --> 00:22:47,640
About the contract...

434
00:22:48,340 --> 00:22:49,740
Now's not the time to get on board.

435
00:22:49,740 --> 00:22:53,400
What is this smell?

436
00:22:54,800 --> 00:22:56,560
Come on, Chief, that's enough.

437
00:22:56,560 --> 00:22:58,580
I actually really like this place.

438
00:22:58,580 --> 00:23:00,160
Really?

439
00:23:00,160 --> 00:23:03,600
Come on, Ryo-san and Chief, stop fighting.

440
00:23:03,600 --> 00:23:05,200
Let's have some tea.

441
00:23:05,200 --> 00:23:06,480
I'll make some right now.

442
00:23:22,000 --> 00:23:36,860
Uuuuuuugh...

443
00:23:36,860 --> 00:23:44,060
If you're interested, please sign with the contract office.
Don't say that, the deal's already fallen through, hasn't it?

444
00:23:44,060 --> 00:23:50,540
But you said you liked it earlier, didn't you?
So, well, come on, just sign.

445
00:23:51,120 --> 00:23:52,620
Give me a campaign discount, come on.

446
00:23:52,620 --> 00:23:54,920
Eeeeh? Me?

447
00:23:56,440 --> 00:23:56,800
Me

448
00:23:57,500 --> 00:23:59,400
Don't say that, just sign it.

449
00:24:05,540 --> 00:24:06,920
What is this randoseru?

450
00:24:07,280 --> 00:24:11,060
It even has a navigation system,
a computer, and a video camera?

451
00:24:11,400 --> 00:24:14,840
Don't elementary schoolers carry
normal notebooks and pencil cases?

452
00:24:15,320 --> 00:24:17,660
Still, I want this randoseru too.

453
00:24:18,160 --> 00:24:20,880
Next time:
Hyper Elementary Schoolboy vs. Ryotsu

454
00:24:21,320 --> 00:24:21,960
See you then!

455
00:24:29,140 --> 00:24:37,760
Even if you stop the clock,
time keeps moving on,

456
00:24:39,380 --> 00:24:47,980
so don't scowl, laugh it off and live on.

457
00:24:49,920 --> 00:24:57,920
Even if today is rainy,

458
00:24:57,920 --> 00:25:03,480
tomorrow will be sunny.

459
00:25:03,480 --> 00:25:08,620
Bye-bye, let's wave goodbye,

460
00:25:08,620 --> 00:25:13,880
farewell to all the bad things.

461
00:25:13,880 --> 00:25:21,500
Oh yeah, let's live however we like,

462
00:25:21,500 --> 00:25:23,960
good things are coming our way.

463
00:25:23,960 --> 00:25:30,280
The sun is calling you through the door.

464
00:25:43,880 --> 00:25:44,000
Thank you for watching.

